      "message": "It\u0027s not really \"setting\" nil multiple times.\nIt IS however checking for each of the various options and ensuring only one of them is specified.\nThe readability argument is valid and maybe I should simply add an explicit check instead:\n```\nfunc ensureOneAndOnly(input ...string) {\n  var already string\n  for _, i :\u003d range input {\n    if i !\u003d \"\" \u0026\u0026 already !\u003d \"\" {\n      panic(fmt.Errorf(\"can\u0027t set both %s and %s\", already, i))\n    }\n    already \u003d i\n  }\n}\nfunc maybe(isSet boolean, arg string) string {\n  if isSet {\n    return arg\n  } else {\n    return \"\"\n}\n```\nThen use those as:\n```\nensureOneAndOnly(\n    buildModeFlag.symlinkForestMarker,\n    buildModeFlag.bp2buildMarker, ...\n    maybe(cmdlineArgs.BazelMode, \"--bazel-mode\"),\n    maybe(cmdlineArgs.BazelModeDev, \"--bazel-mdoe-dev\"))\n// keep the if-else    \nif buildModeFlag.symlinkForestMarker !\u003d \"\" {\n  buildMode \u003d android.SymlinkForest\n} else if ...\n\n```\n\n^ that looks too verbose?\nWhat about I change my func name from `setBuildMode()` to `setBuildModeExclusively()` ?",
